1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,500
That sudden loud roar when you start your car?

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,000
It might not be your muffler.

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,500
A jarring, deep rumble the second the engine turns over—

4
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:08,000
especially if it wasn't there the night before.

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Catalytic converters hold small amounts of precious metal,

6
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,000
which makes them a common target for thieves working fast, underneath the car.

7
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,000
It's become one of the most common theft claims nationwide—

8
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,000
and a stolen converter usually means a full exhaust repair, not a quick patch.

9
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,000
One clue: an etched VIN or a welded shield

10
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
can make your vehicle a harder target, and may help police trace it if it's ever stolen.

11
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,500
Stop by and we'll take a look—

12
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:31,000
Nick's Tire and Auto, on Euclid Avenue.

13
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,000
